  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.1. Increased institutional capacity of employer and business membership organizations (EBMOs)</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Employers Consultative Association of Trinidad and Tobago (ECATT) conducted advocacy activities through the issue of two press releases based on an assessment of the impact of COVID-19 on enterprises. Additionally, they submitted policy recommendations to the National Tripartite Advisory Council in June 2020. These two activities resulted in new economic policy measures such as financial injections to vulnerable sectors announced by the Government in July 2020. The new policy measures also provided grants to small businesses, mostly in tourism, hospitality, retail, transportation, and light manufacturing. In addition, the Government announced in June 2020 the Salary Relief Grant, which included recommendations from ECATT concerning the use of funds from the National Insurance Scheme. The Salary Relief Grants consisted of a fixed amount for workers and those who are unemployed. This fixed amount was given for three months, and in 2021 a one-time grant was also provided.

ECATT based its recommendations on two enterprise surveys it conducted to monitor and track the pandemic&#x2019;s effect on enterprise continuity and survival. The first survey, conducted in May 2020, reached 135 enterprises and the follow-up survey, conducted in March 2021, surveyed over 40 enterprises. It was simultaneous with last COVID-19 spike and the lockdown. 

Based on the survey results and the policy recommendations mentioned above, the ECATT developed and implemented advocacy material, including infographics. In addition, the ECATT used the assessment findings to lobby for government grants, tax relief measures and low-interest rates, amongst others mentioned above. The ILO supported ECATT to develop a customized survey to measure the impact of COVID-19 on enterprises by adapting the ILO enterprise survey tool on &#x201C;Assessing the needs of enterprises resulting from COVID-19&#x201D;. The ILO further supported ECATT to collect data using a digital survey software (Qualtrics), produce the assessment report that was used to develop ECATT&#x2019;s policy recommendations. Additionally, to assist ECATT&#x2019;s advocacy campaign, the ILO developed infographics to present the key findings of the assessment. 

Additionally, the ILO assisted ECATT&#xB4;s capacity development by training one ECATT member in Management of Employers&#xB4; and Business Member Organizations through the Caribbean Academy jointly carried out by the ILO and the ITC-ILO.</narrative>
   </description>
